From: MYOS C2000MAX maintenance
Subject: [PATCH] net: mediatek: reduce contiguous FQ scratch allocations

C2000MAX first boot failed at mtk_open+0x25c in mtk_init_fq_dma:
kcalloc(256, 2048, GFP_KERNEL) needed an order-7 allocation although
the system still had about 38 MiB free.  The live buddy allocator had
no free blocks of 512 KiB or larger.  Opening eth1 after the boot-time
pressure subsided restored a working 1 Gbit/s link.

Use 128 KiB chunks and enlarge the pointer array to preserve its existing
8192-page capacity.  Allocation, descriptor offsets and cleanup already
use MTK_FQ_DMA_LENGTH.  Each chunk remains physically contiguous for
dma_map_single; descriptor counts and total scratch capacity are unchanged.

This is a kernel-side correction pending a newly built kernel and live boot
verification.  The running 0130 kernel has not received this change.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.h
@@ -36,8 +36,8 @@
 #define MTK_TX_DMA_BUF_LEN_V2	0xffff
 #define MTK_QDMA_RING_SIZE	2048
 #define MTK_DMA_SIZE(x)		(SZ_##x)
-#define MTK_FQ_DMA_HEAD		32
-#define MTK_FQ_DMA_LENGTH	256
+#define MTK_FQ_DMA_HEAD		128
+#define MTK_FQ_DMA_LENGTH	64
 #define MTK_NAPI_WEIGHT		256
 #define MTK_RX_ETH_HLEN		(VLAN_ETH_HLEN + VLAN_HLEN + ETH_FCS_LEN)
 #define MTK_RX_HLEN		(NET_SKB_PAD + MTK_RX_ETH_HLEN + NET_IP_ALIGN)
